Subject: Re: Eliminating Reply-to: header -- was: Re: UDB &amp; Multia
In-Reply-To: <199606241225.OAA01979@ceres.tat.physik.uni-tuebingen.de>

> this is a *discussion list* and not a list to distribute questions
> to some answering machines.  for this reason I think it's only reasonable
> that the replies usually should go back to the whole list and not
> only to the original sender.  

Right. That's what the group-reply function in most MUAs is good for.

> but this mailing list won't behave anymore as expected (at least as
> I would expect a discussion list to behave).  please keep your
> reply-to policy as it is right now!

The problem is that with the current policy, I simply *can't* write a private
reply to a message on the list, because both reply and group-reply will direct
a copy to the list.

I am going to use a similar procmail rule (using formail instead of grep). Using procmail
this way only changes the headers in *my* copy of the list, so that reply and group-reply in
elm work again.

cu
Michael

